# git.package.patch

patch a dependency inside the tree via one pre-approved verb; never raw `pnpm patch`. writes a LOCAL PATCH note (who, when, why, upstream).

## flow

begin → edit the files under the edit dir it names → commit

```bash
rhx git.package.patch begin --package is-number --mode apply
echo 'why' | rhx git.package.patch commit --package is-number --why @stdin --upstream <issue-url> --mode apply
```

stage every file commit lists: patch, note, manifest entry, lockfile.

## rules

- plan by default; `--mode apply` acts
- `--why` + `--upstream` required
- edit dir stays in-tree; never the live install, patches dir, or shared store
- several versions installed: `--package <name>@<version>`
- rerun is safe: a sealed patch is a no-op; a lost manifest or lockfile record is refused with the restore step named
- commit makes `pnpm-workspace.yaml` upgrade-safe (`allowUnusedPatches` + `ignorePatchFailures`): an upgrade lands, the stale patch surfaces via `check`

## after the seal

`get` lists each patch · `check` names each stale one + its repair (exit 2) · `del --package <name>[@<version>]` retires one. the onStop hook nudges via `check`, never blocks.

